g first, then EM_ name minus\n  prefix; kind:integer => decimal e_machine. Dispatch on answer_format.kind, never on field name.\n  no .symtab => stripped (answer [] / none / false); no INTERP => static; ET_DYN+INTERP => PIE; ET_REL => object file\n  UPX0/UPX1 sections or \"UPX!\" or entropy>7.2 => PACKED: upx -t F; cp F /tmp/x; upx -d /tmp/x (fix zeroed UPX! first)\nSTEP 3  strings -a -n6 F | grep -m8 -E 'GCC:|clang|rustc|go1\\.|GHC |OCaml|caml_|FPC |Crystal|zig|GNAT Version|gfortran|DMD|Nim|\n        swift|_kDart|kfun:|__svm|MEI|nuitka|AU3!|Borland|MSVBVM|libcob|UPX|HCFG|SENGR'   -> toolchain + blob form\n  toolchain -> tool: Go GoReSym -t -d -p | Rust rustfilt | .NET ilspycmd | jar javap -v -p / jadx | Swift swift-demangle\n  Nim nim-demangle | PyInstaller pyinstxtractor+pycdc | AutoIt autoit-ripper | anything else: rizin -q -c 'aaa;afl' /\n  analyzeHeadless (lib.binary.ghidra_decompile) | foreign arch: rizin -a <arch> / llvm-objdump-18 / Ghidra (no exec, qemu absent)\nHCFG (every new member since D2)\n  python: from lib.binary import hcfg_find, hcfg_scan; hcfg_find(open(F,'rb').read())  -> config, offset, encoding, key, crc_ok\n  raw magic 'HCFG' | b64 'SENGR' | hex '48434647' | rot13 'FRATE' | b64-zlib 'eJ' | b64-gzip 'H4sI' -> covered by hcfg_scan\n  accept only crc32(plain)==header crc AND JSON parses; keep scanning past decoys (D9 had two raw-magic decoys)\n  ALWAYS check the tail: image_end = e_shoff+e_shnum*e_shentsize (or max section/segment end; PE: pefile overlay start);\n  len > image_end => OVERLAY with a day magic (PK19 D19 packed; RS20 D20 = raw HCFG @+48 + scratch, res_len u32@8,\n  scratch_len u16@12, sha256(scratch)@16). o = data.rfind(magic) (\"final\"); parse EVERY header field the QUESTION lists into\n  a dict (size ids = that field, e.g. hcfg_resource_size = u32@8); verify its bounds/sha256; run its transform (D19\n  ror8(b^k2,3)^k1); HCFG at the stated offset. overlay_offset = o, overlay_size = len(data)-o.\n  NOT FOUND => hidden elsewhere: (1) packed? unpack; (2) AES S-box 637c777b / TEA 9e3779b9 / 'expand 32-byte k' => find key+IV\n  near the call, decrypt with pycryptodome; (3) runs of mov [rbp-x], imm => stack-built: collect imms with capstone or\n  emulate the builder with unicorn; (4) PE .rsrc / .NET resource / jar non-class entry / gaps between sections (slack) /\n  custom ELF notes (`readelf -nW`) / compressed `C`-flag sections (`readelf -zx`) / archive appended after the image;\n  (5) .init_array / TLS callback decoder => emulate it. Offsets: raw=the H, base64=the S (GM-confirmed); else first stored byte.\nFIELDS: format = container only (elf/pe/macho?/jar; .NET pe_cli) | machine/architecture = container machine word |\n  qualifier ids dNN_analysis_<tag>_<field> -> member whose file name has <tag> (D15 stripped/symbolized, D16 compact/direct,\n  D21 loader/plugin; match the LONGEST member-name token, a tag may contain `_`); THEN, if >1 member remains, the member the\n  QUESTION names (\"Use the d21-- plugin.cmxs member\", \"basename ends loader.elf\") ; sha256_K = zip archive order |\n  config_* verbatim from HCFG JSON |\n  has_<x>_section = literal section name | hex fields lowercase 0x | never chase the prompt's theme: answer only asked ids.\n  D17 Ada, D18 Fortran, D19 GnuCOBOL, D20 Haskell, D21 OCaml (loader PIE + `.cmxs` ET_DYN plugin; caml_plugin_header,\n  Caml2007D002; HCFG RAW only in the plugin .data): plain ELF -> header ids from the carried-over\n  solver (post first, T+~20 s). The day's twist sits in the NEW field family: read its longest question first -- since D17\n  the question text is an executable spec (rules, offsets, transforms, hashes). `none` only for ABSENT things.\nTHEME FACTS (unasked so far, backfill candidates): every member D2+ embeds a huntress.binary.dynamic_trace.v1 JSON template\n  (branch, event_count, family \"<lang>_<theme>_trace\", effects, network) gated on env HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL. D18 call graph:\n  getenv -> select_string case table -> `mov eax,<fn>; call rax`; D21 NEEDED/dynsym exports/imports + dlopen'd plugin header.\nBACKFILL ids on OLD groups (D8, D17): an unknown field on dNN = that day's own facts. Seen: marker (.huntress string),\n  recover_code (decimal imm), mangled_score_symbol/typeinfo_symbol (bare _ZNK.../_ZTI...; PE .text$/.rdata$), has_go_runtime,\n  has_rust_mangled_symbol, has_coroutine_runtime (enum true/false), methods (Main-Class method_info names incl <init>, JSON),\n  access_flags (decimal, 49), method_count (incl <init>/<clinit>). Derive from bytes, POST all derivable ones together.\nhcfg_storage (enum): base64 carrier -> base64 | literal HCFG in section `.hcfg` -> raw_hcfg_section | in WASM data seg ->\n  wasm_data_segment | in another native data section (.data/.rodata) -> raw_const_array | else raw. Stripped d01 => recover_code none.\nUNGUESSABLE label: ~10 single-id probes max, HELP.md, then re-pull the contract (organizers revise it: enum + rule text).\nFORWARD HINTS: grep each new contract for tokens/days not today's (D19 `RS20 for Day 20` came true; open: enum `neko_bytecode`,\n  \"for Day 26 use the primary classfile named by that unit\" on d07 method_count). Linking themes (D21+): readelf -dW/-rW/-VW.\n```\n\n## Readiness gaps\n```json\n[\n  {\"id\": \"question-layout-parser-mutations\", \"concept\": \"Turn the question's layout prose into a struct and expose EVERY named field (any `<name>_size/_length/_offset/_sha256/_version/_count` id), robust to TT/Mastery mutations of the header\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D20 needed a hand-written branch for the one unknown id (`hcfg_resource_size` = 'HCFG resource length u32le at +8'). Build lib.binary.layout_from_question(text) -> [(name, offset, type)] parsing phrases seen D19-D20: 'Read k1 at +5', 'X length u32le at +8', 'scratch length u16le at +12', 'bytes +16..+47 are the scratch SHA-256', 'the HCFG resource starts at +48, and scratch follows it', 'Verify exact end bounds'; also u8/u16be/u32be/u64le, 'relative to the overlay/file', 'immediately after'. Return a facts dict (fields + derived starts/ends + bound/hash checks) the solver can answer any matching id from by fuzzy name (resource_size == resource length). Fixtures: synthetic overlays with permuted fields, BE ints, renamed magic, extra padding, each with its question text; test that every id resolves.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"contract-revision-watch\", \"concept\": \"Organizers revise the live contract mid-day (D17: exact_text -> enum + rule text)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"When an exact_text label resists ~10 probes: write HELP, then re-pull the contract (`hctf status <id>`) every ~20-30 min and diff question text/answer_format per id; D17 the revision converted ~3.5 h and ~10.9k rejected probes into CORRECT within a minute. Never run mass automated label grouptests on a closed-vocabulary GM field.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"contract-forward-hints\", \"concept\": \"The live contract leaks upcoming days: tokens and day numbers that do not belong to today\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D19 leaked D20's overlay magic ('PK19 for Day 19 or RS20 for Day 20') and it came true. Still open after D21 (D20/D21 contracts added no new token; carried-over questions byte-identical): the format enum lists `neko_bytecode` (unseen), and d07_analysis_method_count says 'for Day 26 use the primary classfile named by that unit'. Each day, grep the contract for magic-like tokens (`[A-Z]{2}\\\\d{2}`), enum values never confirmed, and 'Day NN' > today; record them in solver/NOTES.md and the coverage atlas so the prebuild targets them. The solver maps a `<2 caps><NN>` magic to the group whose day is NN.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"neko-bytecode-member\", \"concept\": \"Neko VM bytecode member (`.n`, magic NEKO): container parse, globals/strings, HCFG location, labels for format/architecture/machine\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"The GM's own format enum (d12-d19 since D19) lists `neko_bytecode` = a Neko member is scheduled. `apt install neko haxe` (candidates neko 2.4.1, haxe 4.3.7) then build fixtures: a Haxe `-neko out.n` program and a raw `nekoc` program holding the HCFG as a string literal (raw bytes and base64 'SENGR...') -- plus `nekotools boot` (Neko standalone ELF = neko VM + appended bytecode, another overlay!). Parser: 'NEKO' u32 nglobals, u32 nfields, u32 codesize; globals (type byte: 1 var, 2 function, 3 string u16/u32 len, 4 float, 5 debug, 6 version), fields (NUL-terminated names), code. Facts: format `neko_bytecode`, globals_count, fields list, string globals, hcfg offset (start of the string payload = the `H`/`S`), has_neko_runtime; architecture/machine for a VM are UNKNOWN -- record candidates (`neko`, `nekovm`, `none`) and read the question text first. Ensure lib.binary magic dispatch and the solver's format() return `neko_bytecode` for raw .n and recognise a nekotools-booted ELF (format elf + overlay).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"theme-facts-recording\", \"concept\": \"Record each day's prompt-theme facts during the single solve (asked on its own day since D19, or in a later backfill)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D5-D18 themes were never asked on their own day, but D19's (overlay_offset/overlay_size, config after unpacking) and D20's (overlay_offset, hcfg_resource_size) WERE and D17 backfilled D1-D7 single-solve facts on their old groups. After CORRECT, spend <=2 min writing the theme facts (stub/overlay header fields, call graph, branch map, imports, trace family/effects, decoder) into solver/NOTES.md under `THEME FACTS dNN:`; the solver's facts dict should already expose them as candidate field names (d19: overlay_version, k1/k2 hex, packed_length, unpacked_size, unpacked_sha256). d20: rs20 version, hcfg_resource_size, scratch_size (35), scratch_sha256, scratch text, image_end, GHC version 9.12.2. d21: loader/plugin NEEDED, plugin exports (caml_plugin_header, caml_globals, camlPlugin_000__entry), Caml2007D002 dynheader unit name Plugin_000, loader dlopen/caml_natdynlink_open imports, trace family ocaml_controlled_dynlink_trace / controlled_library_resolution_only, OCaml 4.02.3.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"native-imports-exports-facts\", \"concept\": \"imports / NEEDED / interpreter / exports lists for ELF, PE, Mach-O\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). Generic facts: ELF `needed` (DT_NEEDED order), `imports` (UND .dynsym names, table order, version suffix stripped), `interpreter` (.interp without NUL), `exports` (defined dynsyms); PE import dll list + functions ... D21 THEME (unasked on D21): loader NEEDED libm/libdl/libc, plugin NEEDED libc + weak __cxa_finalize/__gmon_start__/_ITM_*; expose these for a d21 backfill.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"dynlink-handshake-facts\", \"concept\": \"Loader/plugin handshake facts for a dlopen-style pair (the unasked D21 theme): which member loads which, the dlopen'd path string, dlsym'd symbol names, the plugin's init/registration export and header struct\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D21 = OCaml loader ELF (imports caml_natdynlink_open/caml_dlopen, NEEDED libdl, string 'not an OCaml plugin') + .cmxs plugin exporting caml_plugin_header -> marshalled dynheader with magic `Caml2007D002`, unit list (name `Plugin_000`, crc, defines/imports). Build lib.binary.dynlink_facts(loader, plugin) for (a) OCaml natdynlink (parse caml_plugin_header VA -> file offset, magic, unit names), (b) C dlopen/dlsym (string args near the call: resolve `lea rdi,[rip+x]` before `call dlopen@plt`/`dlsym@plt` with capstone; plugin `plugin_init`/`*_register` exports), (c) PE LoadLibraryA/W + GetProcAddress (string args, DLL export by name/ordinal). Fields: plugin_header_magic, plugin_units (JSON), loaded_library, resolved_symbols (JSON, call order), init_export, plugin_exports (dynsym order, defined only). Fixtures: gcc loader+.so pair with a .hcfg in the .so; synthetic OCaml-shaped .so with a caml_plugin_header pointing at a `Caml2007D002` blob.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"relocation-got-plt-facts\", \"concept\": \"Relocation tables as answers and as storage: .rela.dyn/.rela.plt counts per type (JUMP_SLOT, GLOB_DAT, RELATIVE, IRELATIVE, COPY), PLT slot -> import name, lazy vs BIND_NOW, RELRO, and HCFG pieces reachable only through RELATIVE addends\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Next 'linking' concept after D21 ('mind the boundaries'). lib.binary.elf_reloc_facts(data): per-section relocation list (offset, type name as readelf prints it e.g. R_X86_64_JUMP_SLOT, symbol, addend), counts, plt_imports (JSON in .rela.plt order), bind_now (DT_FLAGS BIND_NOW or DF_1_NOW), relro full/partial/none. Storage twist: a PIE whose HCFG chunks are pointed to by a pointer table filled only by R_X86_64_RELATIVE addends (bytes zero on disk) -> apply relocations to a copy of the image, then hcfg_scan the relocated image; also GOT entries pointing at config. Fixtures via gcc -fPIE -pie / -Wl,-z,now / -Wl,-z,lazy.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"symbol-versioning-interposition\", \"concept\": \"GNU symbol versioning and interposition: .gnu.version/_d/_r, default vs hidden versions (foo@@V2 / foo@V1), binding (GLOBAL/WEAK/LOCAL/UNIQUE), visibility, and LD_PRELOAD-style shims that export libc names\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"lib.binary.elf_version_facts(data): verdefs (name, flags, index), verneeds (file -> [version names]) in table order, per-dynsym version string, weak symbols, interposed libc names (defined dynsyms whose name is a libc import name: open, getenv, dlsym, __libc_start_main) and whether they call dlsym(RTLD_NEXT). Labels as readelf -V / --dyn-syms prints (`GLIBC_2.2.5`, `@@`). Fixtures: gcc -shared with a version script (-Wl,--version-script) defining V1/V2 of a config getter whose V2 returns the HCFG and V1 a decoy; an LD_PRELOAD shim .so.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"library-search-path-facts\", \"concept\": \"How the loader resolves libraries: DT_RPATH vs DT_RUNPATH (incl. $ORIGIN/$LIB tokens), PT_INTERP path, DT_FLAGS_1 (NOW, PIE, NODEFLIB, ORIGIN), SONAME, dlopen path argument absolute/relative\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D21 trace effects = `controlled_library_resolution_only` -> resolution facts are a likely backfill/next-day field family. lib.binary.elf_loader_facts(data): interpreter, needed (order), soname, rpath, runpath (raw string, not expanded), flags/flags_1 token lists as readelf prints them, has_origin. Plus resolve_library(loader, name, members) that maps a NEEDED/dlopen name to the group member that satisfies it (SONAME match first, then basename). Fixtures: gcc -Wl,-rpath,'$ORIGIN/lib' vs --enable-new-dtags, -Wl,-soname, custom --dynamic-linker.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"multi-role-member-router\", \"concept\": \"Groups of 3+ members with roles (loader + several plugins/libraries, stub + payload, client + server), HCFG in one member only, decoy HCFG in another; ids qualified by role or unqualified with the member named in the question text\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D21 needed a hand-written _named_member() for unqualified ids whose question says 'Use the d21-- plugin.cmxs member; the loader has no scored HCFG config' and it had to run AFTER the qualifier peel. Generalize into lib.binary.route_member(group, field, question) -> (member, residual_field): qualifier peel by longest file-name token, then question phrases ('basename ends X', 'Use the dNN-- X member', 'the member that exports Y', 'the library named by the loader's DT_NEEDED', 'the member loaded by ...'), then structural fallbacks (the only member with a crc-valid HCFG for config_*). Regression: D15/D16/D21 shapes + synthetic 3-member groups (loader, plugin_a, plugin_b) with a decoy HCFG (bad crc) in the loader.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"resource-table-overlay\", \"concept\": \"Multi-entry resource directory overlays: magic + count + N fixed-size entries (name/type id, offset