{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QPsYmbd8iyYdVqyA8esZaj","type":"tool_result","content":"challenges/day21/binary-shared-custody/single_solve/work/extracted/evidence/:\nd01--variant-000.elf\nd02--variant-000.elf\nd03--variant-000.dll\nd03--variant-000.runtimeconfig.json\ncontract-forward-hints :: D19 leaked D20's overlay magic ('PK19 for Day 19 or RS20 for Day 20') and it came true. Still open after D21 (D20/D21 contracts added no new token; carried-over questions byte-identical): the format enum lists `neko_bytecode` (unseen), and d07_analysis_method_count says 'for Day 26 use the primary classfile named by that unit'. Each day, grep the contract for magic-like tokens (`[A-Z]{2}\\d{2}`), enum values never confirmed, and 'Day NN' > today; record them in solver/NOTES.md and the coverage atlas so the prebuild targets them. The solver maps a `<2 caps><NN>` magic to the group whose day is NN. \n\ntheme-facts-recording :: D5-D18 themes were never asked on their own day, but D19's (overlay_offset/overlay_size, config after unpacking) and D20's (overlay_offset, hcfg_resource_size) WERE and D17 backfilled D1-D7 single-solve facts on their old groups. After CORRECT, spend <=2 min writing the theme facts (stub/overlay header fields, call graph, branch map, imports, trace family/effects, decoder) into solver/NOTES.md under `THEME FACTS dNN:`; the solver's facts dict should already expose them as candidate field names (d19: overlay_version, k1/k2 hex, packed_length, unpacked_size, unpacked_sha256). d20: rs20 version, hcfg_resource_size, scratch_size (35), scratch_sha256, scratch text, image_end, GHC version 9.12.2. d21: loader/plugin NEEDED, plugin exports (caml_plugin_header, caml_globals, camlPlugin_000__entry), Caml2007D002 dynheader unit name Plugin_000, loader dlopen/caml_natdynlink_open imports, trace fami \n\npe-dll-loader-plugin-pair :: ELF/PE re-rolled per member in Mastery on D2/D4/D10, so a loader/plugin pair may come as PE. l