cept\":\"IL body decoder for 'trace every crossing': per method the call/callvirt/calli/newobj targets (MethodDef/MemberRef/MethodSpec tokens -> Type::Name), ldstr user strings, ldsfld/ldtoken + RuntimeHelpers.InitializeArray (array blobs incl. F# `T<n>_<len>Bytes@` .text data), and which managed methods call each P/Invoke\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Parse method headers (tiny 0x2 / fat 0x3, 12-byte header, extra sections) at RVA, decode the full opcode table (single + 0xFE two-byte), resolve tokens through dnfile tables. Output: call graph edges managed->managed and managed->native (callers of each ImplMap method), user-string list in #US order, array-init blob offsets (maps the D22 HCFG @.text to the field that owns it). Fixtures: same C#/F# projects as dotnet-pinvoke-bridge-facts; verify against `ilspycmd -il`.\"},\n {\"id\":\"jni-java-native-bridge-pair\",\"concept\":\"JVM <-> native FFI pair: jar/class with ACC_NATIVE (0x0100) methods + System.loadLibrary(\\\"x\\\") + a `.so`/`.dll` exporting `Java_<pkg>_<Class>_<method>` (JNI name mangling `_1`=_, `_2`=;, `_3`=[, `_0xxxx`=unicode, `__` overload signature) or JNI_OnLoad + RegisterNatives JNINativeMethod {name, signature, fnPtr} tables\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"lib.binary.jni_bridge_facts(jar_bytes, so_bytes): native methods (class, name, descriptor) from the classfile, loadLibrary argument from the constant pool, exports demangled back to class/method, RegisterNatives triples by scanning .data.rel.ro for (char* name, char* sig, fnptr) with RELATIVE relocs, map each native method -> exported symbol/fn address; HCFG may sit in either member. Fixtures: javac + gcc -shared -I$JAVA_HOME/include (both installed); one static-export lib and one RegisterNatives lib; Kotlin `external fun` variant if kotlinc present.\"},\n {\"id\":\"native-extension-bridges\",\"concept\":\"Script-runtime native extensions as the native side of an FFI bridge: CPython extension `.so` (PyInit_<mod>, PyModuleDef + PyMethodDef table name/flags/doc), Cython (`__pyx_` symbols, embedded .pyx path), ctypes callers (`CDLL(\\\"libx.so\\\")`, argtypes/restype in .pyc constants), cffi (`_cffi_types`), Node N-API `.node` (napi_register_module_v1, node_register_module_v*), Lua `luaopen_<name>`, Ruby `Init_<name>`\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"lib.binary.extension_bridge_facts(data): kind token (python_ext/cython/napi/lua_c/ruby_ext/plain_c), module name from the init export, method table walk via RELATIVE relocs on PyMethodDef[] (name ptr, fn ptr, flags) until NULL, and for a .pyc partner list ctypes library strings + function names. Fixtures: gcc -shared with Python.h (python3-dev present?) else hand-written PyMethodDef struct; N-API shape via plain C exports; Lua shape via luaopen_ export.\"},\n {\"id\":\"dotnet-language-family\",\"concept\":\"Other languages on the .NET runtime as a new-day member and their identity facts: VB.NET (Microsoft.VisualBasic ref, `My` namespace, `_Closure$__`, `VB$` locals), F# (SEEN D22: FSharp.Core AssemblyRef, FSharpSignatureData/OptimizationData.<asm> resources, `$Program`/<StartupCode$...> types, `<>f__AnonymousType<n>`, closures `name@<line>`), C++/CLI, IronPython/PowerShell-compiled\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"lib.binary.dotnet_language_of(data) -> token (csharp/fsharp/vbnet/cppcli) with evidence + language facts dict (FSharp.Core version from AssemblyRef and from the dependency member's AssemblyDef, F# resource names, closure count). Fixtures: `dotnet new console -lang VB` and `-lang F#` (dotnet installed); confirm format pe_cli / machine i386 stay unchanged and HCFG scan hits the F# .text array blob first.\"},\n {\"id\":\"dotnet-primary-support-router\",\"concept\":\"Managed groups with several .dll/.json members: pick the PRIMARY assembly ('primary managed assembly ... dependency DLL members are delivery support only'), expose support-member facts (runtimeconfig tfm/framework name+version, deps.json targets/libraries, dependency AssemblyDef name/version/public key token) and AssemblyRef<->dependency version matching\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Rule: primary = the .dll whose AssemblyDef name is not a framework/dependency name (FSharp.Core, System.*, Microsoft.*, Newtonsoft.*, netstandard) AND that has an entry point or HCFG; tie-break by the question's basename rule. Never scan the 5.7 MB FSharp.Core for HCFG beyond the cheap raw pass. Fixtures: F# console publish output (sample.dll + FSharp.Core.dll + runtimeconfig + deps.json) and a C# app with a ProjectReference library dll.\"},\n {\"id\":\"mixed-mode-native-in-managed\",\"concept\":\"Native code inside or carried by a managed assembly: C++/CLI mixed-mode PE (COR20 ILONLY clear, VTableFixups, native .text alongside IL, machine x86-64/i386 + 32BITREQUIRED), ReadyToRun native code, and shellcode byte[] executed via VirtualAlloc/mmap + Marshal.Copy + GetDelegateForFunctionPointer\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Facts: cor20 flags tokens, vtfixup count/entries, has_native_code; locate a byte[] initialiser (InitializeArray blob) whose callers reach VirtualAlloc/mprotect P/Invokes, disassemble it with capstone in the PE's machine mode and emulate with unicorn for return constants or an HCFG builder. Fixtures: C# with an x86-64 `mov eax, imm; ret` byte[] run through VirtualAlloc/mmap P/Invoke; mixed-mode only synthetically (pefile flag patch) since MSVC is unavailable.\"},\n {\"id\":\"reflection-dynamic-load\",\"concept\":\"Reflection / dynamic loading of a second managed or JVM module: Assembly.Load(byte[]) of a resource or array (Costura.Fody `costura.<name>.dll.compressed` raw-deflate resources, AppDomain.AssemblyResolve), Activator/MethodInfo.Invoke by string name; JVM ClassLoader.defineClass of an embedded (xor/zip) class\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"lib.binary.embedded_modules(data): enumerate .NET ManifestRes